WEBVTT

00:22.040 --> 00:23.680
<i>ONE MORE TIME</i>

00:23.880 --> 00:28.630
I LOOKED AT THE BLOOMING
FLOWERS IN MY SHINING DREAM

00:28.800 --> 00:32.350
<i>NO MORE LIFE</i>
I WAS OBSESSED

00:32.520 --> 00:35.110
MY PAST WAS SCATTERED

00:35.280 --> 00:38.670
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY THOSE HANDS

00:38.840 --> 00:41.990
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
I WAS CALLED

00:42.160 --> 00:45.310
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY A LIGHT SHINING

00:45.480 --> 00:48.710
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
IN THE DARKNESS

00:48.880 --> 00:52.320
<i>ONE MORE TIME</i>
IN THE TWINKLING LIGHT

00:52.480 --> 00:55.440
WATCH THAT FIGURE FADE AWAY

00:55.600 --> 00:59.230
<i>NO MORE LIFE</i>
I WAS LEFT BEHIND

00:59.400 --> 01:02.150
BUT TOMORROW WE'LL MEET AGAIN

01:02.320 --> 01:05.440
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY THOSE HANDS

01:05.600 --> 01:08.750
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
I WAS CALLED

01:08.920 --> 01:12.150
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY A LIGHT SHINING

01:12.320 --> 01:15.470
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
IN THE DARKNESS

01:15.640 --> 01:21.400
SURROUNDED BY THE LIGHT

01:21.560 --> 01:23.840
<i>DON'T CLOSE EYES
HELP ME</i>

01:24.000 --> 01:29.330
WHEN I SCREAM
<i>WILL BE SATISFACTION, YOU KNOW</i>

01:32.820 --> 01:37.040
The seventh month of 1600 AD, or Keicho 5.

01:37.410 --> 01:41.210
Charging Tokugawa Ieyasu with thirteen articles of impeachment,

01:41.210 --> 01:48.130
Ishida Mitsunari sent messengers to various daimyo in the name of the Toyotomi clan,

01:48.130 --> 01:51.300
telling them to raise armies.

01:51.300 --> 01:56.390
At the same time, beings seeking to end the period of turbulence

01:56.390 --> 02:00.270
and build a kingdom to last a thousand years

02:00.270 --> 02:04.520
were about to awaken from a thousand-year sleep.

02:04.520 --> 02:06.520
And then...

02:06.520 --> 02:10.280
On the fifteenth day of the ninth month, at Sekigahara,

02:10.280 --> 02:12.740
the Eastern Army of Tokugawa Ieyasu clashed with

02:12.740 --> 02:17.870
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and Ishida Mitsunari.

02:17.870 --> 02:21.330
As a result of the performance of Kobayakawa Hideaki's troops,

02:21.330 --> 02:27.250
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and
Ishida Mitsunari achieved a sweeping victory,

02:27.250 --> 02:33.510
bringing what should have been
three hundred years of peace to the world.

02:34.340 --> 02:39.390
You should all be quite familiar with this story...

02:46.780 --> 02:50.010
SHOOT THE PAST!

03:08.880 --> 03:10.310
Are you a me from the past?

03:10.480 --> 03:12.040
We look alike, right?

03:12.200 --> 03:14.590
I'm only slightly shorter than you.

03:14.960 --> 03:16.550
I'm still growing up.

03:18.360 --> 03:21.400
So we see illusions in this room?

03:23.160 --> 03:25.720
There is no door, it is indeed an illusion.

03:25.880 --> 03:27.110
It's not.

03:31.640 --> 03:32.640
Too slow!

03:34.160 --> 03:35.560
You have made progress.

03:36.120 --> 03:38.510
I'm proud of my alter ego from the future.

03:39.080 --> 03:42.960
From the future?
You claim to be me from the past?

03:43.480 --> 03:44.960
Exactly.

03:51.480 --> 03:53.630
Is this you from the past?

03:53.800 --> 03:55.710
Yes, for sure.

03:55.880 --> 03:58.270
That's me back in England.

03:58.440 --> 03:59.640
You look alright.

04:00.240 --> 04:01.240
You look okay.

04:01.880 --> 04:03.200
Is Father okay?

04:07.680 --> 04:08.750
What's the matter?

04:09.400 --> 04:11.310
Father is dead.

04:12.400 --> 04:14.310
What? Father is dead?

04:15.120 --> 04:16.270
What happened?

04:18.200 --> 04:19.200
He was killed.

04:32.400 --> 04:33.470
Help me!

04:35.240 --> 04:36.670
Well, well?

04:36.840 --> 04:40.120
I am ashamed of my future self!

04:40.880 --> 04:42.520
You mean...

04:42.680 --> 04:43.910
you're my past self?

04:44.440 --> 04:47.430
Can't you see we are identical?

04:47.600 --> 04:52.550
They say there are three people
in the world with the same face.

04:53.240 --> 04:55.550
You could be the third.

04:56.120 --> 05:00.560
Third? Have you met the second one?

05:00.920 --> 05:04.470
Yes, a great ninja
named Sasuke Sarutobi!

05:05.880 --> 05:07.520
What are you saying?

05:08.240 --> 05:10.280
We are Sasuke Sarutobi!

05:10.720 --> 05:15.190
What? I am Ninjataro, first
disciple of Musashi Miyamoto.

05:15.880 --> 05:17.000
What?

05:17.440 --> 05:19.270
Aren't you me?

05:19.440 --> 05:22.190
You're not Sasuke Sarutobi from the future?

05:22.600 --> 05:25.480
I told you, I am Ninjataro!

05:25.640 --> 05:28.870
Sasuke Sarutobi is at
Princess Kaguya's side.

05:29.040 --> 05:32.190
Past or future, I am Ninjataro!

05:32.960 --> 05:34.390
Stop joking around!

05:34.560 --> 05:36.710
I am Sasuke Sarutobi!

05:37.360 --> 05:40.000
So you must be the
Sasuke from the future!

05:40.640 --> 05:42.680
I don't understand
what you're saying!

05:52.280 --> 05:56.400
Did Musashi manage
to get the artifact?

05:56.560 --> 05:58.120
Probably, but...

05:58.600 --> 05:59.720
But?

05:59.880 --> 06:03.080
Even if we are wary of
Yasha and the ayakashi,

06:04.000 --> 06:09.030
we also must not forget the
traps set by the Yin-Yang monks.

06:09.200 --> 06:10.840
The traps?

06:11.640 --> 06:14.390
To protect the ayakashi artifacts...

06:14.560 --> 06:18.240
from falling into the hands of evil men...

06:18.400 --> 06:21.710
they have placed many traps and spells...

06:21.880 --> 06:24.440
in each of the seven castles.

06:24.600 --> 06:26.800
Is that true?

06:26.960 --> 06:27.960
Yes.

06:28.240 --> 06:32.470
And we're going to one of those castles now.

06:32.640 --> 06:33.790
Indeed.

06:33.960 --> 06:36.190
What if we don't go?

06:36.360 --> 06:38.950
You can stay in Osaka if you want.

06:40.560 --> 06:42.710
I was joking, of course!

06:43.920 --> 06:49.310
I, Danjo, will follow Princess
Kaguya anywhere to protect you!

06:49.480 --> 06:52.470
Thanks, I'm counting on you.

06:53.560 --> 06:54.790
Danjo.

06:55.320 --> 06:56.320
Yes?

06:56.680 --> 07:03.230
I am reassured because you are
always with me, you have my thanks.

07:03.680 --> 07:04.720
That's normal...

07:10.200 --> 07:14.400
Anyway, Sasuke Sarutobi is late.

07:14.560 --> 07:17.790
I hope he was able to
lose Mitsunari Ishida.

07:19.160 --> 07:22.120
Sasuke Sarutobi is already here.

07:23.200 --> 07:24.200
Where?

07:24.280 --> 07:25.480
Here.

07:25.640 --> 07:26.640
But where?

07:27.040 --> 07:29.160
In front of you, Danjo.

07:31.440 --> 07:34.030
A monkey sound?
In front of me?

07:39.080 --> 07:40.430
Princess Kaguya?

07:42.320 --> 07:44.470
Sasuke Sarutobi?

07:49.640 --> 07:51.040
Princess Kaguya?

07:51.200 --> 07:54.160
When were you replaced?

07:54.320 --> 07:55.830
A long time ago!

07:57.160 --> 07:58.310
Sorry.

07:58.480 --> 08:00.590
We've pushed the joke too far.

08:00.600 --> 08:03.040
You got me.

08:15.800 --> 08:18.710
Lord Ryogen, what's wrong?

08:18.880 --> 08:21.350
He's not here yet?

08:21.520 --> 08:23.800
What are you waiting for?

08:25.600 --> 08:28.270
The second artifact, of course!

08:28.840 --> 08:35.030
Right now, Musashi and his
companions are facing Yin-Yang spells.

08:35.640 --> 08:38.950
They probably haven't
gotten their hands on it yet.

08:39.440 --> 08:41.800
How can you be so sure?

08:41.960 --> 08:46.720
Musashi will manage to
overcome these traps easily.

08:47.120 --> 08:49.680
He may not.

08:50.080 --> 08:52.520
Why are you so sure?

08:52.960 --> 08:59.480
Because these traps are made
to disturb the hearts of men.

09:00.160 --> 09:03.230
To disturb the hearts of men?

09:03.600 --> 09:05.480
What do you mean?

09:05.880 --> 09:09.430
These traps pit you
against your own past self.

09:10.000 --> 09:11.400
An alter ego from the past?

09:12.000 --> 09:20.350
It is a secret art of Yin-Yang that alters
space-time and summons your past self.

09:21.000 --> 09:23.360
I'm not interested in how it works!

09:26.000 --> 09:28.200
I'm very interested!

09:29.120 --> 09:31.400
Here you are, Mr. Leonardo da Vinci.

09:32.920 --> 09:37.790
If he is able to alter space-time
and summon your past self,

09:38.720 --> 09:44.390
whoever sealed the artifact
must have been very powerful.

09:44.560 --> 09:46.150
Indeed.

09:46.320 --> 09:50.310
Isn't there a risk of a time paradox?

09:50.480 --> 09:53.760
What on earth are you talking about?

09:54.440 --> 10:01.390
It is this very time paradox
that disturbs the hearts of men.

10:02.200 --> 10:03.240
I see.

10:04.200 --> 10:07.270
Are you hiding something from me?
Yes or no?

10:07.440 --> 10:08.710
Answer me!

10:09.320 --> 10:10.750
No.

10:11.960 --> 10:13.600
That makes me feel better.

10:13.760 --> 10:19.480
I really wouldn't have put up with
you scheming behind my back.

10:24.800 --> 10:27.080
Why are you looking at me like that?

10:29.600 --> 10:30.600
I've had enough.

10:31.360 --> 10:33.670
I always stay at a distance.

10:33.840 --> 10:37.550
I am Tokugawa, the one who should
have been the ruler of the country...

10:37.720 --> 10:40.030
if history had not gone off the rails!

10:43.880 --> 10:45.110
Who did that?

10:45.920 --> 10:49.310
Shingen! Forgive me!
I didn't do it on purpose!

10:49.480 --> 10:51.550
I swear!

10:52.400 --> 10:55.470
So it was you, the shadow of Tokugawa.

10:56.320 --> 10:58.790
The shadow?
So you can talk.

10:58.960 --> 11:00.190
Ieyasu...

11:00.840 --> 11:03.990
You've become quite
proud to talk like that.

11:04.840 --> 11:08.600
Many things have changed since you died.

11:11.480 --> 11:13.150
I apologize.

11:13.320 --> 11:14.390
Whatever.

11:15.480 --> 11:18.310
Just tell me when I'm needed.

11:18.480 --> 11:23.920
I ate a lot of rice cakes and got fat.
I would like to move around a bit.

11:24.360 --> 11:26.750
I can't really tell that you got fatter.

11:27.240 --> 11:32.480
I miss the old days!
I was not as fat and had my youth!

11:32.640 --> 11:34.230
I wish I could go back in time!

11:34.680 --> 11:36.270
That's impossible.

11:36.440 --> 11:37.480
Excuse me?

11:37.640 --> 11:39.230
I have an idea!

11:39.800 --> 11:40.800
Yes?

11:41.440 --> 11:46.710
You can't go back in time,
but you can meet your old self.

11:46.880 --> 11:48.470
What do you say?

11:48.920 --> 11:50.640
Are you interested?

11:50.880 --> 11:53.630
Meet my old self?
Interesting...

11:54.240 --> 11:56.470
Then let's go together!

11:57.480 --> 11:59.760
What?
Are you coming with me?

12:00.320 --> 12:01.590
You don't want me to?

12:01.760 --> 12:03.240
Whatever you want.

12:03.720 --> 12:06.160
You've changed a lot, too.

12:06.480 --> 12:08.920
Let's go see each other younger!

12:28.000 --> 12:29.640
That's a nice gun!

12:30.320 --> 12:33.040
Isn't it?
It was a pain to get it!

12:33.440 --> 12:35.950
Come on, let me hold it for a bit!

12:36.360 --> 12:39.640
No! You can never hold it!

12:40.000 --> 12:41.800
You don't like sharing!

12:42.520 --> 12:45.590
When did I become so selfish?

12:46.280 --> 12:47.950
It's not selfishness!

12:48.480 --> 12:54.550
This is a terrible gun, the demon inside
controls the minds of malicious people!

12:55.080 --> 12:57.520
Yet you seem fine.

12:57.880 --> 13:01.510
Yes, my heart is transparent,
like the water of a lake.

13:02.440 --> 13:04.110
Then I'm safe!

13:04.560 --> 13:05.760
True.

13:05.840 --> 13:08.200
See? Let me hold it!

13:08.360 --> 13:10.320
No! Never!

13:10.960 --> 13:12.160
Why?

13:12.880 --> 13:21.310
If you touch it, you go to another world
and you could be killed by a demon there.

13:35.160 --> 13:37.910
Killed?
You are still alive.

13:38.320 --> 13:41.200
Enough!
I won't let you hold it!

13:41.600 --> 13:45.390
Yeah, you're pretty selfish!
I feel sorry for myself.

13:46.400 --> 13:51.470
Anyway, wait a few years and you
will get it from Master Takuan.

13:52.040 --> 13:53.680
For now, it's no!

13:57.960 --> 13:59.440
Got it.

14:00.200 --> 14:05.950
In that case, I'll take it from
you after you bite the dust!

14:10.040 --> 14:15.040
By the way, have you ever
met Musashi, the castle thief?

14:15.200 --> 14:16.840
Yes.

14:17.400 --> 14:19.870
- Did you shoot him?
- No.

14:20.840 --> 14:22.190
What do you mean?

14:22.560 --> 14:26.960
You haven't forgotten that you were
assigned to kill Musashi Miyamoto?

14:27.160 --> 14:28.300
I forgot.

14:28.440 --> 14:29.520
What?

14:29.520 --> 14:34.510
I see. You're me just after
I got that assassination order.

14:35.400 --> 14:36.550
Exactly!

14:36.720 --> 14:43.270
The shogunate promised me a job for
the head of the thief Musashi Miyamoto.

14:43.440 --> 14:45.000
I am looking for him.

14:45.960 --> 14:48.600
I hope to stop living in misery.

14:48.760 --> 14:52.990
That's why I have to find
Musashi at all costs!

14:53.720 --> 14:55.120
I applaud your efforts.

14:55.280 --> 15:00.040
Very soon you will find
Musashi and confront him.

15:00.320 --> 15:03.070
- Nevertheless...
- No, I will be defeated?

15:03.240 --> 15:04.310
No.

15:05.920 --> 15:07.800
Did you win and let him get away?

15:07.960 --> 15:09.950
- No.
- Then what?

15:11.280 --> 15:13.920
Musashi is now a valuable companion.

15:14.880 --> 15:15.920
What?

15:16.680 --> 15:18.880
And we rob castles together.

15:21.640 --> 15:24.870
Of course, a lot has happened in between.

15:25.320 --> 15:27.550
You'll figure it out eventually.

15:27.960 --> 15:30.240
Bastard, you're making fun of me!

15:31.560 --> 15:32.760
Oh my!

15:33.640 --> 15:37.920
You forgot your mission,
and rob castles with Musashi.

15:38.840 --> 15:42.230
You're a disgrace to your
samurai rank! I will kill you!

15:46.000 --> 15:48.120
Father was killed?

15:48.280 --> 15:50.840
What happened?

15:51.400 --> 15:54.150
A lot happened after I came here.

15:55.160 --> 15:57.600
Did you find the name of the murderer?

15:58.040 --> 15:59.440
Yes.

15:59.600 --> 16:01.720
It's Musashi Miyamoto!

16:02.120 --> 16:03.710
Miss Desperado!

16:04.440 --> 16:06.510
You killed him, right?

16:06.800 --> 16:09.550
- Not yet.
- Why not?

16:10.280 --> 16:14.240
Because Musashi is very strong!

16:14.560 --> 16:17.920
I knew I was no match for him.

16:18.680 --> 16:19.880
This is ridiculous!

16:20.400 --> 16:27.840
Musashi and his companions
keep claiming he's innocent.

16:28.800 --> 16:32.840
At first I didn't believe it, of course.

16:33.560 --> 16:36.550
But lately, I've been having doubts.

16:37.320 --> 16:45.030
Indeed, Miss Desperado, there is
no way Musashi killed your father.

16:45.880 --> 16:49.710
Please tell Musashi about your doubts.

16:50.680 --> 16:55.670
You can then become a full-fledged friend.

16:56.320 --> 16:59.550
Wait a second! What did you just say?

16:59.720 --> 17:01.680
A full-fledged friend?

17:02.440 --> 17:07.030
Yes, right now, Musashi is in this castle.

17:07.480 --> 17:11.160
Desperado is also accompanying Musashi.

17:12.280 --> 17:15.670
I'm not officially accompanying him!

17:25.000 --> 17:31.470
I see. If I understand correctly, you're going
to become friends with our father's killer.

17:32.360 --> 17:34.110
I said no...

17:41.800 --> 17:43.790
- Miss Desperado!
- Yes?

17:44.480 --> 17:47.870
I was not talking to you,
but to the one from the past.

17:48.360 --> 17:49.840
This is too complicated!

17:50.560 --> 17:57.040
Soon everything will be easier,
because I'm going to kill you.

18:02.000 --> 18:05.790
The future me should be in front of me.

18:05.960 --> 18:10.950
Yet you claim to not be Sasuke
Sarutobi, but Ninjataro.

18:11.440 --> 18:15.120
I am Ninjataro!
I have always been!

18:15.280 --> 18:16.840
I will always be!

18:17.280 --> 18:22.510
Have you lost your memory?
But your ninja art is terrible.

18:25.040 --> 18:33.670
All I can think of is that you assassinated
Sasuke Sarutobi and took his place.

18:34.600 --> 18:37.190
Assassinated?
Not at all!

18:37.360 --> 18:40.190
Sasuke Sarutobi is alive and well!

18:40.880 --> 18:44.510
Even if he was temporarily
transformed into a monkey.

18:44.680 --> 18:47.960
But he is alive, no doubt about it!

18:48.280 --> 18:50.430
Why would I believe you?

18:52.560 --> 18:54.200
Wait!

18:55.000 --> 18:58.870
If you are a real ninja, fight like one!

19:00.520 --> 19:04.350
Impossible, you are
much stronger than me!

19:04.840 --> 19:06.320
Then die!

19:23.160 --> 19:24.560
You are strong!

19:24.960 --> 19:28.030
Of course!
I've been training hard!

19:39.480 --> 19:41.630
I expected no less.

19:42.320 --> 19:43.470
You've made progress!

19:44.560 --> 19:47.200
Nothing beats daily practice!

19:47.400 --> 19:50.440
If you live long enough,
you can do it too!

19:58.960 --> 20:01.270
Why are you so weak?

20:02.040 --> 20:03.270
Because...

20:08.640 --> 20:12.160
You're doing well.
You must have practiced.

20:12.920 --> 20:14.720
I haven't practiced!

20:14.880 --> 20:17.840
I had to learn how to survive!

20:18.600 --> 20:19.600
Miss Desperado!

20:20.040 --> 20:21.240
Do your best!

20:22.040 --> 20:23.040
Thanks!

20:24.240 --> 20:25.990
This is too complicated...

20:31.480 --> 20:32.710
We're here.

20:32.880 --> 20:34.630
Yes, this is it.

20:35.080 --> 20:38.150
There is no anti-ayakashi
device. Let's go.

20:38.480 --> 20:39.580
Wait!

20:43.360 --> 20:46.160
Don't walk so close to me,
you're getting in the way!

20:46.320 --> 20:48.150
But I'm afraid...

20:48.600 --> 20:51.400
Your face makes me afraid.

21:06.480 --> 21:08.280
You are strong!
I got defeated!

21:09.240 --> 21:14.230
I'd love to chat about the past
with you, but I have to leave.

21:15.160 --> 21:18.710
Tell me how to get out of this room.

21:18.880 --> 21:20.200
Very simple.

21:20.840 --> 21:22.320
Just kill me.

21:22.480 --> 21:24.680
Then the door will open.

21:25.520 --> 21:26.640
What?

21:27.240 --> 21:29.520
Killing my past self?

21:29.800 --> 21:33.400
It seems that this is the only way out.

21:34.920 --> 21:38.800
But I'm your past.
In other words, if you kill me...

21:40.040 --> 21:43.920
you will probably disappear
from this world.

21:44.080 --> 21:45.480
This is insane!

21:46.360 --> 21:48.240
This is a time paradox.

21:48.400 --> 21:49.910
A logical contradiction.

21:51.240 --> 21:56.870
But you and I are not subject
to this logic, apparently.

21:57.400 --> 22:00.360
Because I am not your past self.

22:07.880 --> 22:09.360
I see.

22:10.200 --> 22:16.750
Killing your past self erases everything
that happened up to the present.

22:17.360 --> 22:20.320
By exploiting this time paradox...

22:20.480 --> 22:28.350
you disturb the hearts of those who have
entered that room until they go mad.

22:29.040 --> 22:33.310
The Yin-Yang monks who designed
that room must have been powerful.

22:33.880 --> 22:35.080
Indeed.

22:35.240 --> 22:38.040
I must leave now.

22:38.640 --> 22:42.270
To get the second artifact?

22:42.840 --> 22:44.720
Of course.

22:44.880 --> 22:51.750
But before that, I want to see how
Musashi will get out of this trap.

22:53.600 --> 22:56.720
I look forward to your report.

23:13.160 --> 23:15.750
That is me, but younger!

23:15.920 --> 23:17.670
I recognize myself too!

23:20.040 --> 23:23.590
To get out of here,
I have to kill my old self?

23:24.920 --> 23:30.560
But if I do that,
it will mean killing myself!

23:31.000 --> 23:32.720
What should I do?

23:35.480 --> 23:38.230
There must be a way!

23:38.760 --> 23:40.990
But I don't know it!

23:41.560 --> 23:44.000
I'm in a panic!

23:51.400 --> 23:53.910
But what should I do?

24:23.440 --> 24:25.190
MAKE HASTE

24:25.360 --> 24:27.160
THROUGH THE CROWDS

24:27.320 --> 24:31.080
THEY'RE CUTTING OFF YOUR ESCAPE

24:31.240 --> 24:34.950
IN THIS TWILIGHT TOWN
I HEAR PIERCING SOUNDS

24:35.120 --> 24:38.880
LIKE A WANDERING CAT

24:39.040 --> 24:40.790
WITHOUT KNOWING

24:40.960 --> 24:42.760
WHERE TO GO

24:42.920 --> 24:46.680
I'M TRAPPED IN THIS TOWN THAT NEVER SLEEPS

24:46.840 --> 24:50.360
MY REFLECTION IN THE MIRROR

24:50.520 --> 24:55.200
SEEING MYSELF TRANSFORM

24:55.360 --> 24:57.720
I'M HOLDING ON

24:57.880 --> 25:01.160
FOR AS LONG AS POSSIBLE

25:03.200 --> 25:07.830
I'LL SHOW YOU THAT I CAN

25:08.000 --> 25:10.560
WIN OVER THIS TOWN

25:11.720 --> 25:13.760
FROM MY BURNING HEART

25:13.920 --> 25:15.910
SHINE SO MANY

25:16.080 --> 25:19.870
DAZZLING COLORS AND LIGHTS

25:20.040 --> 25:21.550
FLOODING ALL OVER

25:21.720 --> 25:23.710
SCATTERING ALL OVER

25:23.880 --> 25:27.030
SURROUNDING ME

25:27.200 --> 25:29.650
SOLEMNLY

25:31.600 --> 25:36.000
Hey, Yin-Yang monk,
you built this castle!

25:36.600 --> 25:39.490
This little game has
gone on for long enough!

25:40.320 --> 25:43.710
The next chapter: <i>Riddle Sorcerer</i>!
